# Repo-level kill switch for the preview owner cutover.
#
# deploy/deploy-docker.sh sources this file for the effective
# PREVIEW_CONNECTION_MODE unless the environment (or ~/ops/deploy.env) already
# sets it:
#
#   owner  — the machine preview tunnels and the preview content hosts
#            (preview-<uuid>.<SITES_DOMAIN>) are served by the independently
#            released preview-connection service. Ordinary app releases never
#            touch it, so a deploy no longer drops a preview tunnel or a Vite
#            HMR socket. The business backend runs with PREVIEW_CONNECTION_MODE
#            = owner and PREVIEW_CONNECTION_URL set from the compose file.
#
#   legacy — the business backend keeps serving previews in-process, exactly as
#            before the cutover. The next deploy writes the routing back (the
#            tunnel through app-router, content hosts on the backend) and does
#            not start the owner, so setting this file to legacy is a complete,
#            no-box-access revert. Routes only change on a deploy; a running
#            helper is not disturbed in between.
#
# A box without the standing api-front (ACTIVE_BACKEND_DIR unset) is always
# forced to legacy: it has no route to the owner, so it must not render a
# backend in owner mode.
PREVIEW_CONNECTION_MODE=owner
